      <t:profileDesc xmlns:t="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
         <t:abstract>
            <t:p>
               The work referred to as ‘gadl’ of ʾAlāniqos is currently attested uniquely in <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ANLcr23">Rome, Biblioteca dell’Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei, Conti Rossini 23</t:ref>, where it consists of a chronology of Ethiopian
               kings, twelve miracles,
                a malkǝʾ-hymn to Taṭamqa Madḫǝn, a disciple of ʾAlāniqos, and a spiritual genealogy
                of Ethiopian monks. It does not contain a
                vita proper (see    <t:bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/BWJEWURQ"><seg type="journalArticle"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Marrassini1982Alaniqos"/><title level="a">Il &lt;hi rend="italics"&gt;Gadla Alāniqos&lt;/hi&gt;</title><title level="j">Egitto e Vicino Oriente</title><author><t:forename>Paolo</t:forename><t:surname>Marrassini</t:surname></author><date>1982</date><biblScope unit="volume">5</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">143-182</biblScope></t:bibl>).
            </t:p>
         </t:abstract>
